  "worked_solution": "Along the curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=3{t}^{2},\\,y(t)=3\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t,\\,z(t)=3\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t.\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{\u2032}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t)\\,k \\\\  & =6t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t\\,j-3\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}x\\,dx-z\\,dy+y\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt-z\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt+y\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-z\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+y\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }3{t}^{2}\\cdot (6t)-3\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t\\cdot (3\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t)+3\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t\\cdot (-3\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t)\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }18{t}^{3}-9{cos}^{2}\u2061t-9{sin}^{2}\u2061t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }18{t}^{3}-9\\,dt \\\\  & =(\\frac{9{t}^{4}}{2}-9t){|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =72{\\pi }^{4}-18\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$",
